IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `salsl-dates`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1987 (SA), with the Long Service Leave Regulations 2017 where they fill in the Act (reg 4 and
-- Schedule 1: the forms of the records and of the statements given to the worker). THE RULES, seat-neutral. The
-- questions of the worker are in salsl-seat.l4, which restates none of these.
--
-- Answers are named outcomes (some carrying a number of weeks, an amount or a date), never MAYBE BOOLEAN. Where the
-- text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, "does not apply", "is not entitled ... if", "only arises", an
-- "if" or "where" condition, a period fixed in its own words) the outcome begins "no"; where a provision's own scope
-- does not reach the case and the Act says nothing more, the outcome says so ("does not reach this"). Judgments the
-- Act leaves to SAET or to an inspector are inputs, and the outcome is stated on the condition.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (the Act's current
-- version, 1.7.2017, and the Regulations' current version, 1.9.2017, as the register's unauthorised RTFs). State of
-- South Australia, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Long Service Leave Act 1987 -- the rules`

§§ `ss 3, 9, 16 -- whom the Act covers`

-- s 3(1): "worker means a person employed under a contract of service" (a "means" definition).
-- s 16: "This Act does not apply in relation to workers who have a long service leave entitlement -- (a) under some
-- other Act; or (b) under a fair work instrument under the Fair Work Act 2009 of the Commonwealth; or (c) under an
-- instrument given continuing effect under the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act
-- 2009 of the Commonwealth."
-- s 9(3), (5): a SAET determination that a class of workers' entitlements "will be determined by reference to a
-- particular award, agreement or scheme rather than by reference to this Act" has effect in accordance with its terms;
-- entitlements under it "are enforceable as if they had arisen under this Act".
DECLARE `Other long service leave entitlement` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `an entitlement under another Act`
    `an entitlement under a fair work instrument under the Fair Work Act 2009 of the Commonwealth`
    `an entitlement under an instrument given continuing effect under the Fair Work transitional Act 2009 of the Commonwealth`

DECLARE `Coverage answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: the Act applies to workers, and a worker means a person employed under a contract of service (s 3(1)); a contractor engaged under a contract for services is not one`
    `no: the Act does not apply to a worker with a long service leave entitlement under some other Act (s 16(a))`
    `no: the Act does not apply to a worker with a long service leave entitlement under a fair work instrument under the Fair Work Act 2009 of the Commonwealth, such as a modern award or enterprise agreement that provides it (s 16(b))`
    `no: the Act does not apply to a worker with a long service leave entitlement under an instrument given continuing effect under the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009 of the Commonwealth (s 16(c))`
    `yes, but under a SAET determination your long service leave is worked out by reference to the award, agreement or scheme it names, and that entitlement is enforceable as if it arose under this Act (s 9(3), (5))`
    `yes: you are a worker and the Act applies to you (ss 3(1), 16)`

GIVEN `employed under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the other entitlement` IS AN `Other long service leave entitlement`,
      `a SAET determination applies to my class of workers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Coverage answer`
`the coverage answer for` `employed under a contract of service` `other` `the other entitlement` `determination` `a SAET determination applies to my class of workers` MEANS
    IF NOT `employed under a contract of service`
    THEN `no: the Act applies to workers, and a worker means a person employed under a contract of service (s 3(1)); a contractor engaged under a contract for services is not one`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the other entitlement`
         WHEN `an entitlement under another Act` THEN `no: the Act does not apply to a worker with a long service leave entitlement under some other Act (s 16(a))`
         WHEN `an entitlement under a fair work instrument under the Fair Work Act 2009 of the Commonwealth` THEN `no: the Act does not apply to a worker with a long service leave entitlement under a fair work instrument under the Fair Work Act 2009 of the Commonwealth, such as a modern award or enterprise agreement that provides it (s 16(b))`
         WHEN `an entitlement under an instrument given continuing effect under the Fair Work transitional Act 2009 of the Commonwealth` THEN `no: the Act does not apply to a worker with a long service leave entitlement under an instrument given continuing effect under the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009 of the Commonwealth (s 16(c))`
         OTHERWISE
            IF `a SAET determination applies to my class of workers`
            THEN `yes, but under a SAET determination your long service leave is worked out by reference to the award, agreement or scheme it names, and that entitlement is enforceable as if it arose under this Act (s 9(3), (5))`
            ELSE `yes: you are a worker and the Act applies to you (ss 3(1), 16)`

§§ `s 4 -- service in and outside the State`

-- s 4(1): "Subject to this section, a worker's long service leave entitlement accrues under this Act in respect of --
-- (a) service in the State; (b) service outside the State where the worker is predominantly employed in the State; (c)
-- service outside the State in pursuance of a contract of employment of which South Australia law is the proper law."
-- The list is not closed with "only": service outside all three is "not reached" (fork F3).
-- s 4(2): "Where a worker would, but for this subsection, have a long service leave entitlement both under this Act
-- and a corresponding law, the worker may elect to take the entitlement under this Act or under the corresponding law,
-- but not under both."
DECLARE `Place of service` IS ONE OF
    `in South Australia`
    `outside South Australia while predominantly employed in South Australia`
    `outside South Australia under a contract of employment whose proper law is South Australian law`
    `outside South Australia otherwise`

DECLARE `Accrual answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: this service accrues long service leave under the Act, s 4(1) paragraph` HAS `the paragraph` IS A STRING
    `yes, this service accrues under s 4(1), but as you also have an entitlement under a corresponding law (of the Commonwealth, another State or Territory, or another country) you may elect to take it under this Act or under that law, not both (s 4(2)); s 4(1) paragraph` HAS `the paragraph` IS A STRING
    `s 4(1) does not reach this service: it lists service in South Australia, service outside it while predominantly employed in it, and service outside it under a contract governed by South Australian law, and the Act says nothing of other service`

GIVEN `the place` IS A `Place of service`
GIVETH A STRING
`the s 4(1) paragraph for` `the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `in South Australia` THEN "(a)"
    WHEN `outside South Australia while predominantly employed in South Australia` THEN "(b)"
    WHEN `outside South Australia under a contract of employment whose proper law is South Australian law` THEN "(c)"
    OTHERWISE ""

GIVEN `the place` IS A `Place of service`, `also under a corresponding law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Accrual answer`
`the s 4 answer for` `the place` `corresponding law` `also under a corresponding law` MEANS
    IF `the place` EQUALS `outside South Australia otherwise`
    THEN `s 4(1) does not reach this service: it lists service in South Australia, service outside it while predominantly employed in it, and service outside it under a contract governed by South Australian law, and the Act says nothing of other service`
    ELSE IF `also under a corresponding law`
         THEN `yes, this service accrues under s 4(1), but as you also have an entitlement under a corresponding law (of the Commonwealth, another State or Territory, or another country) you may elect to take it under this Act or under that law, not both (s 4(2)); s 4(1) paragraph` (`the s 4(1) paragraph for` `the place`)
         ELSE `yes: this service accrues long service leave under the Act, s 4(1) paragraph` (`the s 4(1) paragraph for` `the place`)

§§ `s 6(1), (2) -- breaks and absences`

-- s 6(1): "A worker's continuity of service is not affected by -- (a) subject to an order of SAET to the contrary, a
-- break in the worker's service brought about by the employer where the worker is re-employed pursuant to an order of
-- a court or SAET; (b) a break ... brought about by the employer in an attempt to avoid an obligation or liability ...;
-- (c) absence ... in accordance with the contract of service; (d) absence ... on account of illness or injury; (e)
-- absence ... on account of long service leave or annual leave; (f) absence ... on any other kind of leave; (g) the
-- standing down of the worker by the employer on account of slackness in trade where the worker is subsequently
-- re-employed by the employer; (h) a break ... arising directly or indirectly from an industrial dispute where the
-- worker returns to work in accordance with the terms of settlement of the dispute or is re-employed by the employer
-- when the dispute is settled; (i) any other break in the worker's service brought about by the employer where the
-- worker returns to work or is re-employed by the employer within two months."
-- s 6(2): "Where a worker's continuity of service ... is preserved under subsection (1)(f), (g), (h) or (i), the period
-- of absence or the duration of the break from work is not to be taken into account in calculating the period of the
-- worker's service with the employer."
DECLARE `Kind of break` IS ONE OF
    `a break my employer brought about, after which I was re-employed under an order of a court or SAET`
    `a break my employer brought about to avoid an obligation under the Act or a long service leave award, agreement or scheme`
    `an absence allowed by my contract of service`
    `an absence through illness or injury`
    `long service leave or annual leave`
    `another kind of leave`
    `a stand-down by my employer for slackness in trade, after which I was re-employed by that employer`
    `a break arising from an industrial dispute, after which I returned under the settlement or was re-employed when it was settled`
    `another break my employer brought about, after which I returned or was re-employed by that employer`
    `a break I brought about myself, such as resigning, after which I was re-employed`

DECLARE `Continuity answer` IS ONE OF
    `continuous, and the time counts as service: s 6(1) paragraph` HAS `the paragraph` IS A STRING
    `continuous, but the time away is not counted in your period of service: s 6(1) and (2), paragraph` HAS `the paragraph` IS A STRING
    `no: SAET has ordered that this break does affect your continuity of service (s 6(1)(a))`
    `no: s 6(1)(i) preserves continuity only where you return or are re-employed within two months of the break; the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `s 6(1) does not reach a break you brought about yourself, and the Act says nothing more; service must be continuous (s 3(1), service), so check whether another paragraph applies`

GIVEN `the break` IS A `Kind of break`,
      `SAET has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the first day of the break` IS A DATE,
      `the day I returned` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Continuity answer`
`the s 6 answer for` `the break` `SAET ordered otherwise` `SAET has ordered otherwise` `from` `the first day of the break` `returned` `the day I returned` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the break`
    WHEN `a break my employer brought about, after which I was re-employed under an order of a court or SAET` THEN
        IF `SAET has ordered otherwise`
        THEN `no: SAET has ordered that this break does affect your continuity of service (s 6(1)(a))`
        ELSE `continuous, and the time counts as service: s 6(1) paragraph` "(a)"
    WHEN `a break my employer brought about to avoid an obligation under the Act or a long service leave award, agreement or scheme` THEN `continuous, and the time counts as service: s 6(1) paragraph` "(b)"
    WHEN `an absence allowed by my contract of service` THEN `continuous, and the time counts as service: s 6(1) paragraph` "(c)"
    WHEN `an absence through illness or injury` THEN `continuous, and the time counts as service: s 6(1) paragraph` "(d)"
    WHEN `long service leave or annual leave` THEN `continuous, and the time counts as service: s 6(1) paragraph` "(e)"
    WHEN `another kind of leave` THEN `continuous, but the time away is not counted in your period of service: s 6(1) and (2), paragraph` "(f)"
    WHEN `a stand-down by my employer for slackness in trade, after which I was re-employed by that employer` THEN `continuous, but the time away is not counted in your period of service: s 6(1) and (2), paragraph` "(g)"
    WHEN `a break arising from an industrial dispute, after which I returned under the settlement or was re-employed when it was settled` THEN `continuous, but the time away is not counted in your period of service: s 6(1) and (2), paragraph` "(h)"
    WHEN `another break my employer brought about, after which I returned or was re-employed by that employer` THEN
        IF `the day I returned` `is on or before` `the s 6(1)(i) last day`
        THEN `continuous, but the time away is not counted in your period of service: s 6(1) and (2), paragraph` "(i)"
        ELSE `no: s 6(1)(i) preserves continuity only where you return or are re-employed within two months of the break; the last day was` `the s 6(1)(i) last day`
    OTHERWISE `s 6(1) does not reach a break you brought about yourself, and the Act says nothing more; service must be continuous (s 3(1), service), so check whether another paragraph applies`
    WHERE
        -- Fork F4: "within two months" runs from the first day of the break.
        `the s 6(1)(i) last day` MEANS `the first day of the break` `plus months` 2

§§ `ss 3(3), 6(3), 6(4) -- other periods that count as service`

-- s 3(1): "service means continuous service with the same employer or with related employers under a contract of
-- service or a series of contracts of service" (a "means" definition). s 3(3): "Employers are related ... if -- (a) one
-- takes over or otherwise acquires the business or part of the business of the other; or (b) they are related
-- corporations; or (c) a series of relationships can be traced between them under paragraph (a) or (b)."
-- s 6(3): "Where a worker enters into a contract of service with an employer within 12 months after the completion of
-- an apprenticeship with the employer, the period of apprenticeship will be taken into account ...".
-- s 6(4): "Where a worker enters into service as a member of the Armed Forces of the Commonwealth (not being service as
-- a member of the Permanent Forces), that period of service will be regarded as service with the employer by whom the
-- worker was last employed."
DECLARE `Other period` IS ONE OF
    `an apprenticeship with this employer`
    `service in the Armed Forces of the Commonwealth, other than the Permanent Forces`
    `service in the Permanent Forces`
    `service with an employer that took over or acquired the business, or part of it, of the other`
    `service with a related corporation`
    `service with a chain of such employers`
    `service with an unrelated employer`

DECLARE `Counting answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it counts as service, under` HAS `the provision` IS A STRING
    `no: the contract with the employer was entered into more than 12 months after the apprenticeship was completed (s 6(3)); the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no: service in the Permanent Forces is excepted (s 6(4))`
    `no: service means continuous service with the same employer or with related employers (s 3(1)), and this employer is neither`

GIVEN `the period` IS AN `Other period`,
      `the day the apprenticeship was completed` IS A DATE,
      `the day the contract of service was entered into` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Counting answer`
`the counting answer for` `the period` `apprenticeship completed` `the day the apprenticeship was completed` `contract entered` `the day the contract of service was entered into` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period`
    WHEN `an apprenticeship with this employer` THEN
        IF `the day the contract of service was entered into` `is on or before` `the s 6(3) last day`
        THEN `yes: it counts as service, under` "s 6(3)"
        ELSE `no: the contract with the employer was entered into more than 12 months after the apprenticeship was completed (s 6(3)); the last day was` `the s 6(3) last day`
    WHEN `service in the Armed Forces of the Commonwealth, other than the Permanent Forces` THEN `yes: it counts as service, under` "s 6(4), as service with the employer by whom you were last employed"
    WHEN `service in the Permanent Forces` THEN `no: service in the Permanent Forces is excepted (s 6(4))`
    WHEN `service with an employer that took over or acquired the business, or part of it, of the other` THEN `yes: it counts as service, under` "s 3(1) (service) and s 3(3)(a), as long as it is continuous"
    WHEN `service with a related corporation` THEN `yes: it counts as service, under` "s 3(1) (service) and s 3(3)(b), as long as it is continuous"
    WHEN `service with a chain of such employers` THEN `yes: it counts as service, under` "s 3(1) (service) and s 3(3)(c), as long as it is continuous"
    OTHERWISE `no: service means continuous service with the same employer or with related employers (s 3(1)), and this employer is neither`
    WHERE
        -- Fork F1: "within 12 months after the completion" ends on the same day 12 months later.
        `the s 6(3) last day` MEANS `the day the apprenticeship was completed` `plus months` 12

§§ `s 5(7) with s 6 -- completed years of service`

-- s 5(7): "An entitlement under this section only arises in respect of completed years of service." Days that s 6(2)
-- leaves out move the first day later; days that s 6(3) or (4) adds move it earlier (fork F2).
GIVEN `the first day of service` IS A DATE,
      `the day of reckoning` IS A DATE,
      `the days not counted` IS A NUMBER,
      `the days added` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the completed years of service from` `the first day of service` `to` `the day of reckoning` `less` `the days not counted` `plus` `the days added` MEANS
    `the completed years from` (`the first day of service` `plus days` (`the days not counted` MINUS `the days added`)) `to` `the day of reckoning`

-- A number of years given as a plain number is rounded down: only completed years count (s 5(7)).
GIVEN `the years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the completed years in` `the years` MEANS `the larger of` 0 `and` (FLOOR `the years`)

§§ `s 5(1), (6) -- the entitlement`

-- s 5(1): "Subject to this Act, a worker who has 10 years or more service is entitled to the following long service
-- leave -- (a) 13 weeks leave in respect of the first 10 years of service; and (b) 1.3 weeks leave in respect of each
-- subsequent year of service." 13 weeks for 10 years is 1.3 weeks a year, so the two paragraphs give 1.3 weeks for each
-- completed year from 10 years (finding 2).
-- s 5(6): "Where long service leave has been taken by a worker or a payment in lieu of long service leave has been made
-- to a worker, the worker's long service leave entitlement is reduced accordingly."
GIVEN `the completed years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 5(1) weeks for` `the completed years` MEANS
    IF `the completed years` AT LEAST 10
    THEN 13 PLUS (1.3 TIMES (`the completed years` MINUS 10))
    ELSE 0

DECLARE `Entitlement answer` IS ONE OF
    `entitled (s 5(1)): the weeks accrued, and the weeks remaining after leave taken and payments in lieu (s 5(6)), are` HAS `the weeks accrued` IS A NUMBER, `the weeks remaining` IS A NUMBER
    `no: the entitlement to long service leave arises at 10 years of service (s 5(1)), and your completed years are` HAS `the completed years` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the years` IS A NUMBER, `the weeks used` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Entitlement answer`
`the s 5(1) answer for` `the years` `used` `the weeks used` MEANS
    IF `the years counted` AT LEAST 10
    THEN `entitled (s 5(1)): the weeks accrued, and the weeks remaining after leave taken and payments in lieu (s 5(6)), are` (`the s 5(1) weeks for` `the years counted`) (`the larger of` 0 `and` ((`the s 5(1) weeks for` `the years counted`) MINUS `the weeks used`))
    ELSE `no: the entitlement to long service leave arises at 10 years of service (s 5(1)), and your completed years are` `the years counted`
    WHERE
        `the years counted` MEANS `the completed years in` `the years`

§§ `ss 5(2)-(5), (7) -- when service ends`

-- s 5(2): "Where the service of a worker who is entitled to long service leave is terminated, the worker is entitled to
-- a payment in lieu of long service leave." s 5(3): "Subject to subsection (4), a worker who has completed seven years
-- service (but less than 10 years service) is, on termination of the worker's service, entitled to a payment equal to
-- the monetary equivalent of 1.3 weeks leave in respect of each completed year of service." s 5(4): "A worker is not
-- entitled to a payment under subsection (3) if -- (a) the worker's contract of service is terminated on the ground of
-- serious and wilful misconduct on the part of the worker; or (b) the contract of service is unlawfully terminated by
-- the worker." s 5(5): "Where a worker's service is terminated by the worker's death, the worker's entitlement under
-- this section vests in his or her personal representative."
DECLARE `How service ended` IS ONE OF
    `I resigned lawfully`
    `I ended my contract unlawfully`
    `my employer ended it, not for misconduct`
    `my employer ended it on the ground of my serious and wilful misconduct`
    `I retired`
    `the worker died`

DECLARE `Termination answer` IS ONE OF
    `a payment in lieu of your long service leave (s 5(2)), in weeks of your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the termination (s 8(4)(a))` HAS `the weeks` IS A NUMBER
    `a payment of the monetary equivalent of 1.3 weeks leave for each completed year of service (s 5(3)), in weeks of your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the termination (s 8(4)(a))` HAS `the weeks` IS A NUMBER
    `the entitlement vests in the personal representative of the worker who died (s 5(5)), in weeks of the ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the death (s 8(4)(a)), to be paid on request (s 8(4)(b)); weeks and provision` HAS `the weeks` IS A NUMBER, `the provision` IS A STRING
    `no: there is no payment under s 5(3), as the contract was terminated on the ground of serious and wilful misconduct (s 5(4)(a))`
    `no: there is no payment under s 5(3), as you terminated the contract unlawfully (s 5(4)(b))`
    `no: a payment on termination arises only from seven completed years of service (s 5(3), (7)), and the completed years are` HAS `the completed years` IS A NUMBER
    `no: the leave already taken and payments in lieu already made use up the entitlement (s 5(6))`

GIVEN `the years` IS A NUMBER, `the ending` IS A `How service ended`, `the weeks used` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Termination answer`
`the s 5 termination answer for` `the years` `ended by` `the ending` `used` `the weeks used` MEANS
    IF `the years counted` AT LEAST 10
    THEN IF `the weeks owed` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN IF `the ending` EQUALS `the worker died`
              THEN `the entitlement vests in the personal representative of the worker who died (s 5(5)), in weeks of the ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the death (s 8(4)(a)), to be paid on request (s 8(4)(b)); weeks and provision` `the weeks owed` "s 5(2)"
              ELSE `a payment in lieu of your long service leave (s 5(2)), in weeks of your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the termination (s 8(4)(a))` `the weeks owed`
         ELSE `no: the leave already taken and payments in lieu already made use up the entitlement (s 5(6))`
    ELSE IF `the years counted` AT LEAST 7
         THEN BRANCH
                IF `the ending` EQUALS `my employer ended it on the ground of my serious and wilful misconduct`
                THEN `no: there is no payment under s 5(3), as the contract was terminated on the ground of serious and wilful misconduct (s 5(4)(a))`
                IF `the ending` EQUALS `I ended my contract unlawfully`
                THEN `no: there is no payment under s 5(3), as you terminated the contract unlawfully (s 5(4)(b))`
                IF `the weeks owed` AT MOST 0
                THEN `no: the leave already taken and payments in lieu already made use up the entitlement (s 5(6))`
                IF `the ending` EQUALS `the worker died`
                THEN `the entitlement vests in the personal representative of the worker who died (s 5(5)), in weeks of the ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the death (s 8(4)(a)), to be paid on request (s 8(4)(b)); weeks and provision` `the weeks owed` "s 5(3)"
                OTHERWISE `a payment of the monetary equivalent of 1.3 weeks leave for each completed year of service (s 5(3)), in weeks of your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the termination (s 8(4)(a))` `the weeks owed`
         ELSE `no: a payment on termination arises only from seven completed years of service (s 5(3), (7)), and the completed years are` `the years counted`
    WHERE
        `the years counted` MEANS `the completed years in` `the years`
        -- s 5(1) and s 5(3) both come to 1.3 weeks for each completed year; s 5(6) takes off what was used (fork F6).
        `the weeks owed` MEANS (1.3 TIMES `the years counted`) MINUS `the weeks used`

§§ `s 5(1a) with ss 8(3a), 10(2a), (7) -- cashing out leave by agreement`

-- s 5(1a): "A worker who is entitled to long service leave under subsection (1) becomes entitled to a payment in lieu
-- of the long service leave or a part of the long service leave if an individual agreement to that effect is made and
-- recorded in writing and signed by the employer and the worker after the entitlement to the leave accrues to the
-- worker."
DECLARE `Cashing out answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are entitled to the payment in lieu (s 5(1a)); it is worked out at your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before it is made, without accommodation (s 8(3a)(a)); a change in your rate within the period of the leave cashed out brings a further payment (s 8(3a)(b)); your employer must give you a copy of the signed record (s 10(2a)(b)) and a statement in Form 3 of the Regulations of the leave cashed out and the days remaining (s 10(7), reg 4(4))`
    `no: only a worker entitled to long service leave under s 5(1), from 10 years of service, can cash it out (s 5(1a)); your completed years are` HAS `the completed years` IS A NUMBER
    `no: the agreement must be an individual agreement, negotiated between you and your employer (s 5(1a); s 3(1), individual agreement)`
    `no: the agreement must be recorded in writing and signed by both you and your employer (s 5(1a))`
    `no: the agreement must be made after the entitlement to the leave cashed out has accrued to you (s 5(1a))`

GIVEN `the years` IS A NUMBER,
      `it is an individual agreement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it is in writing signed by both` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it was made after the leave accrued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Cashing out answer`
`the s 5(1a) answer for` `the years` `individual` `it is an individual agreement` `written` `it is in writing signed by both` `after accrual` `it was made after the leave accrued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the completed years in` `the years` LESS THAN 10
        THEN `no: only a worker entitled to long service leave under s 5(1), from 10 years of service, can cash it out (s 5(1a)); your completed years are` (`the completed years in` `the years`)
        IF NOT `it is an individual agreement`
        THEN `no: the agreement must be an individual agreement, negotiated between you and your employer (s 5(1a); s 3(1), individual agreement)`
        IF NOT `it is in writing signed by both`
        THEN `no: the agreement must be recorded in writing and signed by both you and your employer (s 5(1a))`
        IF NOT `it was made after the leave accrued`
        THEN `no: the agreement must be made after the entitlement to the leave cashed out has accrued to you (s 5(1a))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you are entitled to the payment in lieu (s 5(1a)); it is worked out at your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before it is made, without accommodation (s 8(3a)(a)); a change in your rate within the period of the leave cashed out brings a further payment (s 8(3a)(b)); your employer must give you a copy of the signed record (s 10(2a)(b)) and a statement in Form 3 of the Regulations of the leave cashed out and the days remaining (s 10(7), reg 4(4))`

§§ `s 3(2), (4) -- the ordinary weekly rate of pay`

-- s 3(2): the ordinary weekly rate of pay is "the worker's weekly rate of pay as at the relevant date exclusive of
-- overtime, shift premiums and penalty rates", but (a) on commission or payment by result, "averaging the worker's
-- weekly earnings over the 12 months immediately preceding the relevant date"; (b) if at any time in the three years
-- before the relevant date the worker was on an hourly rate, had varied ordinary hours, or worked casual or part-time,
-- "averaging the number of hours worked per week in that period of three years and multiplying that result by the
-- worker's rate of pay per hour as at the relevant date"; (c) if the employer provides accommodation during employment
-- but not on leave, the rate "will be increased by an amount representing the weekly value of that accommodation".
-- s 3(4): weeks of whole-week unpaid leave and weeks of absence on account of a work injury with weekly payments under
-- the Return to Work Act 2014 (or, before 1 July 2015, the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1986) are
-- disregarded, and the periods are taken to total 12 months or 3 years of the remaining weeks; paid leave counts.
-- s 8(3a)(a): a payment in lieu by agreement is worked out "not so as to include any amount representing the value of
-- accommodation". Fork F7: the person states the weeks counted and the earnings or hours in them.
DECLARE `Basis of pay` IS ONE OF
    `a weekly rate`
    `commission or another system of payment by result`
    `hourly, varied ordinary hours, casual or part-time at some time in the last three years`

DECLARE `Purpose of the rate` IS ONE OF
    `long service leave`
    `a payment in lieu by agreement`
    `a payment in lieu on termination`

DECLARE `Rate answer` IS ONE OF
    `your ordinary weekly rate of pay, in dollars a week, and the provision, are` HAS `the rate` IS A NUMBER, `the provision` IS A STRING
    `it cannot be worked out: averaging under s 3(2)(a) or (b) needs at least one week counted (s 3(4))`

GIVEN `the basis` IS A `Basis of pay`,
      `the weekly rate` IS A NUMBER,
      `the earnings in the weeks counted` IS A NUMBER,
      `the hours in the weeks counted` IS A NUMBER,
      `the weeks counted` IS A NUMBER,
      `the hourly rate` IS A NUMBER,
      `accommodation is provided at work but not on leave` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the weekly value of the accommodation` IS A NUMBER,
      `the purpose` IS A `Purpose of the rate`
GIVETH A `Rate answer`
`the s 3(2) rate for` `the basis` `weekly` `the weekly rate` `earnings` `the earnings in the weeks counted` `hours` `the hours in the weeks counted` `weeks` `the weeks counted` `hourly` `the hourly rate` `accommodation` `accommodation is provided at work but not on leave` `value` `the weekly value of the accommodation` `for` `the purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the basis`
    WHEN `a weekly rate` THEN `your ordinary weekly rate of pay, in dollars a week, and the provision, are` (`the weekly rate` PLUS `the accommodation`) (CONCAT "s 3(2)", `the accommodation note`)
    WHEN `commission or another system of payment by result` THEN
        IF `the weeks counted` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN `your ordinary weekly rate of pay, in dollars a week, and the provision, are` ((`the earnings in the weeks counted` DIVIDED BY `the weeks counted`) PLUS `the accommodation`) (CONCAT "s 3(2)(a), (4)", `the accommodation note`)
        ELSE `it cannot be worked out: averaging under s 3(2)(a) or (b) needs at least one week counted (s 3(4))`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the weeks counted` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN `your ordinary weekly rate of pay, in dollars a week, and the provision, are` (((`the hours in the weeks counted` DIVIDED BY `the weeks counted`) TIMES `the hourly rate`) PLUS `the accommodation`) (CONCAT "s 3(2)(b), (4)", `the accommodation note`)
        ELSE `it cannot be worked out: averaging under s 3(2)(a) or (b) needs at least one week counted (s 3(4))`
    WHERE
        `the accommodation counts` MEANS
                `accommodation is provided at work but not on leave`
            AND (NOT (`the purpose` EQUALS `a payment in lieu by agreement`))
        `the accommodation` MEANS IF `the accommodation counts` THEN `the weekly value of the accommodation` ELSE 0
        `the accommodation note` MEANS
            IF `the accommodation counts`
            THEN ", with the weekly value of accommodation added under s 3(2)(c)"
            ELSE IF `accommodation is provided at work but not on leave`
                 THEN ", without the value of accommodation (s 8(3a)(a))"
                 ELSE ""

§§ `ss 7(3), (4), (7), 8(1), (2) -- taking and paying the leave`

-- s 7(3): "The employer should give a worker at least 60 days notice of the date from which leave is to be taken."
-- s 7(4)(c): the employer and the worker "may agree on ... the granting and taking of long service leave on less than 60
-- days notice". "Should", not "must" (finding 1). Fork F8: notice given on a day counts if the leave starts 60 or more
-- days after it.
DECLARE `Notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `enough: at least 60 days notice (s 7(3)); the latest day for the notice was` HAS `the latest day` IS A DATE
    `shorter notice is allowed, as you and your employer agreed to it (s 7(4)(c))`
    `less than the 60 days notice s 7(3) says your employer should give; the latest day for the notice was` HAS `the latest day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the day of the notice` IS A DATE, `the first day of leave` IS A DATE, `we agreed to shorter notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`the s 7(3) answer for notice on` `the day of the notice` `leave from` `the first day of leave` `agreed` `we agreed to shorter notice` MEANS
    IF `the day of the notice` `is on or before` `the latest day`
    THEN `enough: at least 60 days notice (s 7(3)); the latest day for the notice was` `the latest day`
    ELSE IF `we agreed to shorter notice`
         THEN `shorter notice is allowed, as you and your employer agreed to it (s 7(4)(c))`
         ELSE `less than the 60 days notice s 7(3) says your employer should give; the latest day for the notice was` `the latest day`
    WHERE
        `the latest day` MEANS `the first day of leave` `plus days` (0 MINUS 60)

-- s 7(7): "Every day occurring after the commencement of a period of long service leave (including public holidays and
-- days on which the worker would not normally have been required to work) will be counted as a day of that leave."
GIVEN `the first day of leave` IS A DATE, `the days of leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 7(7) last day of leave from` `the first day of leave` `for` `the days of leave` MEANS
    `the first day of leave` `plus days` (`the days of leave` MINUS 1)

-- s 8(1): "a worker who is on long service leave is entitled to be paid at his or her ordinary weekly rate of pay".
GIVEN `the weeks` IS A NUMBER, `the rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 8 amount for` `the weeks` `at` `the rate` MEANS `the weeks` TIMES `the rate`

-- s 8(2): "Payment for a period of long service leave must be made in one of the following ways -- (a) in advance for
-- the whole period of leave; or (b) on the same days as payment of wages would have been made if the worker remained at
-- work (in which case payment must, at the written request of the worker, be made by cheque posted to an address
-- specified by the worker); or (c) in some other way agreed between the employer and the worker." A closed list.
DECLARE `Way of paying leave` IS ONE OF
    `in advance for the whole period of leave`
    `on my usual paydays`
    `another way my employer and I agreed`
    `another way I did not agree to`

DECLARE `Way of paying answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a way s 8(2) allows, paragraph` HAS `the paragraph` IS A STRING
    `yes: a way s 8(2) allows, paragraph (b); as you asked in writing, it must be paid by cheque posted to the address you gave (s 8(2)(b))`
    `no: payment must be made in advance, on the usual paydays, or in another way you and your employer agreed (s 8(2))`

GIVEN `the way` IS A `Way of paying leave`, `I asked in writing for a posted cheque` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Way of paying answer`
`the s 8(2) answer for` `the way` `cheque` `I asked in writing for a posted cheque` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way`
    WHEN `in advance for the whole period of leave` THEN `yes: a way s 8(2) allows, paragraph` "(a)"
    WHEN `on my usual paydays` THEN
        IF `I asked in writing for a posted cheque`
        THEN `yes: a way s 8(2) allows, paragraph (b); as you asked in writing, it must be paid by cheque posted to the address you gave (s 8(2)(b))`
        ELSE `yes: a way s 8(2) allows, paragraph` "(b)"
    WHEN `another way my employer and I agreed` THEN `yes: a way s 8(2) allows, paragraph` "(c)"
    OTHERWISE `no: payment must be made in advance, on the usual paydays, or in another way you and your employer agreed (s 8(2))`

§§ `s 8(3), (3a)(b) -- a change in the rate of pay`

-- s 8(3): "If a variation in a worker's rate of pay occurs while the worker is on leave, that variation must be
-- reflected in the payment for the leave and if payment has been made in advance, the employer must, on the worker's
-- return to work, make any adjustment necessary to give effect to the variation." s 8(3a)(b): a payment in lieu by
-- agreement "must, if a variation in the worker's rate of pay occurs during the period from the date of the payment of
-- a duration equal to the period of leave in lieu of which the payment is made, be followed by a further payment to
-- the worker that reflects the variation in the rate of pay."
DECLARE `Kind of leave payment` IS ONE OF
    `leave paid in advance`
    `leave paid on the usual paydays`
    `a payment in lieu by agreement`

DECLARE `Variation answer` IS ONE OF
    `the variation must be reflected in your leave pay (s 8(3)); the difference, in dollars, is` HAS `the difference` IS A NUMBER
    `your employer must make the adjustment on your return to work (s 8(3)); the difference, in dollars, is` HAS `the difference` IS A NUMBER
    `your employer must make a further payment that reflects the variation (s 8(3a)(b)), in dollars` HAS `the difference` IS A NUMBER
    `s 8(3a)(b) requires a further payment to you; it does not say that a fall in your rate is recovered from you`
    `no: s 8(3a)(b) reaches a variation only within the period, from the payment, equal to the leave cashed out`
    `no variation: the rate did not change`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of leave payment`,
      `the old rate` IS A NUMBER,
      `the new rate` IS A NUMBER,
      `the weeks after the variation` IS A NUMBER,
      `the variation fell within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Variation answer`
`the s 8(3) answer for` `the kind` `from` `the old rate` `to` `the new rate` `weeks` `the weeks after the variation` `within` `the variation fell within the period` MEANS
    IF `the new rate` EQUALS `the old rate`
    THEN `no variation: the rate did not change`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the kind`
         WHEN `leave paid in advance` THEN `your employer must make the adjustment on your return to work (s 8(3)); the difference, in dollars, is` `the difference`
         WHEN `leave paid on the usual paydays` THEN `the variation must be reflected in your leave pay (s 8(3)); the difference, in dollars, is` `the difference`
         OTHERWISE
            IF NOT `the variation fell within the period`
            THEN `no: s 8(3a)(b) reaches a variation only within the period, from the payment, equal to the leave cashed out`
            ELSE IF `the difference` GREATER THAN 0
                 THEN `your employer must make a further payment that reflects the variation (s 8(3a)(b)), in dollars` `the difference`
                 ELSE `s 8(3a)(b) requires a further payment to you; it does not say that a fall in your rate is recovered from you`
    WHERE
        -- Fork F9: the difference is the change in the weekly rate times the weeks of leave after the change.
        `the difference` MEANS (`the new rate` MINUS `the old rate`) TIMES `the weeks after the variation`

§§ `s 7(6) -- leave taken in anticipation, then the service ends`

-- s 7(6): "If -- (a) a worker takes long service leave in anticipation of the entitlement to that leave accruing to the
-- worker; and (b) before the entitlement to that leave accrues, the service of the worker is terminated (for any
-- reason), the employer may deduct from any remuneration payable to the worker on the termination of service the
-- difference between the amount paid to the worker in respect of the long service leave taken and the amount of
-- payment in lieu of long service leave (if any) to which the worker would have been entitled on the termination of
-- service if the worker had not taken leave in anticipation of the entitlement accruing."
DECLARE `Deduction answer` IS ONE OF
    `your employer may deduct up to this amount, in dollars, from the remuneration payable to you on termination (s 7(6))` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `nothing may be deducted: what you were paid for the leave is no more than the payment in lieu you would have had (s 7(6))`
    `no: s 7(6) applies only where you took the leave in anticipation of the entitlement accruing`
    `no: s 7(6) applies only where the service ended before the entitlement to the leave accrued`

GIVEN `I took leave in anticipation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the service ended before it accrued` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the amount paid for the leave` IS A NUMBER,
      `the payment in lieu I would have had` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Deduction answer`
`the s 7(6) answer for` `I took leave in anticipation` `ended before accrual` `the service ended before it accrued` `paid` `the amount paid for the leave` `would have had` `the payment in lieu I would have had` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `I took leave in anticipation`
        THEN `no: s 7(6) applies only where you took the leave in anticipation of the entitlement accruing`
        IF NOT `the service ended before it accrued`
        THEN `no: s 7(6) applies only where the service ended before the entitlement to the leave accrued`
        IF `the amount paid for the leave` GREATER THAN `the payment in lieu I would have had`
        THEN `your employer may deduct up to this amount, in dollars, from the remuneration payable to you on termination (s 7(6))` (`the amount paid for the leave` MINUS `the payment in lieu I would have had`)
        OTHERWISE `nothing may be deducted: what you were paid for the leave is no more than the payment in lieu you would have had (s 7(6))`

§§ `The regulative rules and their deadlines`

DECLARE `Leave party` IS ONE OF
    `the worker`
    `the employer`
    `the applicant for the worker`

DECLARE `Leave act` IS ONE OF
    `pay the payment in lieu of long service leave`
    `give the worker the statement of the leave to be taken`
    `grant the leave or make the payment directed by the inspector`
    `apply to SAET for an order`
    `engage in other employment in place of the employment`

-- s 8(4)(b): a payment in lieu on termination "must be made to the worker immediately on the termination or, if the
-- worker has died, to the personal representative of the worker on request." Fork F10: "immediately" is the day of the
-- termination (or of the request); day 0 is that day.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Leave party` `Leave act`
`s 8(4)(b) -- the payment in lieu must be made immediately on the termination` MEANS
    PARTY  `the employer`
    MUST   `pay the payment in lieu of long service leave`
    WITHIN 0
    LEST   BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 8(4)(b): the payment in lieu of long service leave was not made immediately on the termination (or on the personal representative's request)"

-- s 10(6): "Where a worker has been granted long service leave, the employer must, before the leave is taken, give to
-- the worker a statement in the prescribed form setting out the number of days of leave to be taken and the number of
-- days of leave (if any) that will remain due to the worker at the conclusion of the leave. Maximum penalty: $200."
-- The prescribed form is Form 2 of Schedule 1 to the Regulations (reg 4(3)). Day 0 is the day the leave was granted;
-- the last day is the day before the leave starts.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Leave party` `Leave act`
`s 10(6) -- the statement must be given before the leave is taken` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the employer`
    MUST   `give the worker the statement of the leave to be taken`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 10(6): the statement in Form 2 was not given before the leave was taken (maximum penalty $200)"

-- s 12(1): the inspector "may, by notice in writing, direct the employer to grant the long service leave or to make the
-- payment within a period (not being less than 14 days) stated in the notice". s 12(6)(a): failing to comply (no
-- review having been sought) is an offence, maximum penalty $5 000. Fork F11: day 0 is the day the employer received
-- the notice.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Leave party` `Leave act`
`s 12(1) -- the employer must comply with the inspector's notice within the period stated` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the employer`
    MUST   `grant the leave or make the payment directed by the inspector`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 12(6)(a): the employer did not comply with the inspector's notice within the period stated (maximum penalty $5 000)"

-- s 13(4): "An order cannot be made under this section if the service of the worker was terminated more than three
-- years before the date of the application." Day 0 is the day the service was terminated; the last day is the same day
-- three years later (fork F1).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Leave party` `Leave act`
`s 13(4) -- the application must be made within three years of the termination` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the applicant for the worker`
    MUST   `apply to SAET for an order`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the applicant for the worker` BECAUSE "s 13(4): the service of the worker was terminated more than three years before the application, so no order can be made"

-- s 14(1): "A worker must not, while on long service leave, engage in any other employment in place of the employment
-- in relation to which the right to leave accrued. Maximum penalty: $1 000." Day 0 is the first day of leave; the
-- prohibition runs to the last day of the leave.
GIVEN `the last day of leave counted from 0` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Leave party` `Leave act`
`s 14(1) -- no other employment in place of the employment while on leave` `the last day of leave counted from 0` MEANS
    PARTY  `the worker`
    SHANT  `engage in other employment in place of the employment`
    WITHIN `the last day of leave counted from 0`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the worker` BECAUSE "s 14(1): the worker engaged in other employment in place of the employment while on long service leave (maximum penalty $1 000)"

DECLARE `Deadline answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: done on or before the last day, which was` HAS `the last day allowed` IS A DATE
    `late: done after the last day, which was` HAS `the last day allowed` IS A DATE
    `not yet done, and still in time: the last day is` HAS `the last day allowed` IS A DATE
    `not yet done, and the last day has passed: it was` HAS `the last day allowed` IS A DATE

-- On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED
-- means in time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it today would still be in
-- time. A day before the clock start is taken as day 0. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Leave party` `Leave act`
      `the party` IS A `Leave party`
      `the act` IS A `Leave act`
      `the clock start` IS A DATE
      `the final day` IS A DATE
      `it has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was done` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Deadline answer`
`the deadline answer for` `the rule` `by` `the party` `doing` `the act` `from` `the clock start` `ending` `the final day` `done` `it has been done` `on` `the day it was done` `as of` `today` MEANS
    IF `it has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the party` `the act` (`the larger of` 0 `and` (`the days from` `the clock start` `to` `the day it was done`))))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `in time: done on or before the last day, which was` `the final day`
         OTHERWISE `late: done after the last day, which was` `the final day`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the party` `the act` (`the larger of` 0 `and` (`the days from` `the clock start` `to` `today`))))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `not yet done, and still in time: the last day is` `the final day`
         OTHERWISE `not yet done, and the last day has passed: it was` `the final day`

§§ `s 8(4)(b) -- when the payment on termination is due`

DECLARE `Payment timing answer` IS ONE OF
    `paid in time: on the day of the termination, as s 8(4)(b) requires`
    `paid late: s 8(4)(b) requires payment immediately on the termination, which was on` HAS `the day due` IS A DATE
    `not yet paid, and overdue: s 8(4)(b) required payment immediately on the termination, which was on` HAS `the day due` IS A DATE
    `due today: s 8(4)(b) requires payment immediately on the termination`
    `paid in time: on the day the personal representative asked, as s 8(4)(b) requires`
    `paid late: s 8(4)(b) requires payment to the personal representative on request, which was made on` HAS `the day due` IS A DATE
    `not yet paid, and overdue: s 8(4)(b) required payment to the personal representative on request, which was made on` HAS `the day due` IS A DATE
    `due today: s 8(4)(b) requires payment to the personal representative on request`
    `not yet due: after a death the payment is made to the personal representative on request (s 8(4)(b)), and no request has been made`

GIVEN `the day of the termination` IS A DATE,
      `the worker died` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the personal representative has asked` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day of the request` IS A DATE,
      `it has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day it was paid` IS A DATE,
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Payment timing answer`
`the s 8(4)(b) answer for` `the day of the termination` `died` `the worker died` `asked` `the personal representative has asked` `on` `the day of the request` `paid` `it has been paid` `on` `the day it was paid` `as of` `today` MEANS
    IF `the worker died` AND (NOT `the personal representative has asked`)
    THEN `not yet due: after a death the payment is made to the personal representative on request (s 8(4)(b)), and no request has been made`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the deadline answer for` `s 8(4)(b) -- the payment in lieu must be made immediately on the termination` `by` `the employer` `doing` `pay the payment in lieu of long service leave` `from` `the day it falls due` `ending` `the day it falls due` `done` `it has been paid` `on` `the day it was paid` `as of` `today`
         WHEN `in time: done on or before the last day, which was` d THEN
            IF `the worker died`
            THEN `paid in time: on the day the personal representative asked, as s 8(4)(b) requires`
            ELSE `paid in time: on the day of the termination, as s 8(4)(b) requires`
         WHEN `late: done after the last day, which was` d THEN
            IF `the worker died`
            THEN `paid late: s 8(4)(b) requires payment to the personal representative on request, which was made on` d
            ELSE `paid late: s 8(4)(b) requires payment immediately on the termination, which was on` d
         WHEN `not yet done, and still in time: the last day is` d THEN
            IF `the worker died`
            THEN `due today: s 8(4)(b) requires payment to the personal representative on request`
            ELSE `due today: s 8(4)(b) requires payment immediately on the termination`
         OTHERWISE
            IF `the worker died`
            THEN `not yet paid, and overdue: s 8(4)(b) required payment to the personal representative on request, which was made on` `the day it falls due`
            ELSE `not yet paid, and overdue: s 8(4)(b) required payment immediately on the termination, which was on` `the day it falls due`
    WHERE
        `the day it falls due` MEANS IF `the worker died` THEN `the day of the request` ELSE `the day of the termination`

§§ `s 10(6) -- the statement before leave`

DECLARE `Statement answer` IS ONE OF
    `the statement was given in time, before the leave started (s 10(6)); the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the statement was not given before the leave started, as s 10(6) requires (maximum penalty $200); the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `not yet given, and still in time: your employer must give it, in Form 2 of the Regulations, by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the day the leave was granted` IS A DATE,
      `the first day of leave` IS A DATE,
      `it has been given` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day it was given` IS A DATE,
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Statement answer`
`the s 10(6) answer for leave granted on` `the day the leave was granted` `starting` `the first day of leave` `given` `it has been given` `on` `the day it was given` `as of` `today` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the deadline answer for` (`s 10(6) -- the statement must be given before the leave is taken` (`the days from` `the day the leave was granted` `to` `the s 10(6) last day`)) `by` `the employer` `doing` `give the worker the statement of the leave to be taken` `from` `the day the leave was granted` `ending` `the s 10(6) last day` `done` `it has been given` `on` `the day it was given` `as of` `today`
    WHEN `in time: done on or before the last day, which was` d THEN `the statement was given in time, before the leave started (s 10(6)); the last day was` d
    WHEN `not yet done, and still in time: the last day is` d THEN `not yet given, and still in time: your employer must give it, in Form 2 of the Regulations, by` d
    OTHERWISE `the statement was not given before the leave started, as s 10(6) requires (maximum penalty $200); the last day was` `the s 10(6) last day`
    WHERE
        `the s 10(6) last day` MEANS `the first day of leave` `plus days` (0 MINUS 1)

§§ `s 14(1) -- other work while on leave`

DECLARE `Other work answer` IS ONE OF
    `the Act does not forbid this: s 14(1) forbids only other employment in place of the employment in which the leave accrued`
    `no: you must not, while on long service leave, engage in other employment in place of your employment (s 14(1)); this work began during the leave, which is an offence (maximum penalty $1 000); the leave ends on` HAS `the last day of leave` IS A DATE
    `s 14(1) does not reach this work: it begins after your leave ends, on` HAS `the last day of leave` IS A DATE
    `s 14(1) does not reach work that began before your leave; it does forbid going on with it during the leave in place of your employment`

GIVEN `the first day of leave` IS A DATE,
      `the days of leave` IS A NUMBER,
      `the work is in place of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the first day of the work` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Other work answer`
`the s 14(1) answer for leave from` `the first day of leave` `for` `the days of leave` `in place` `the work is in place of my employment` `work from` `the first day of the work` MEANS
    IF NOT `the work is in place of my employment`
    THEN `the Act does not forbid this: s 14(1) forbids only other employment in place of the employment in which the leave accrued`
    ELSE IF `the first day of the work` `is before` `the first day of leave`
         THEN `s 14(1) does not reach work that began before your leave; it does forbid going on with it during the leave in place of your employment`
         ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 14(1) -- no other employment in place of the employment while on leave` (`the days of leave` MINUS 1)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `engage in other employment in place of the employment` (`the days from` `the first day of leave` `to` `the first day of the work`)))
              WHEN FULFILLED THEN `s 14(1) does not reach this work: it begins after your leave ends, on` `the s 14 last day`
              OTHERWISE `no: you must not, while on long service leave, engage in other employment in place of your employment (s 14(1)); this work began during the leave, which is an offence (maximum penalty $1 000); the leave ends on` `the s 14 last day`
    WHERE
        `the s 14 last day` MEANS `the s 7(7) last day of leave from` `the first day of leave` `for` `the days of leave`

§§ `s 10(2)(c), (5) -- the records`

-- s 10(2)(c): the record "must be kept throughout the period of the worker's service and for at least three years
-- after the termination of that service". s 10(5): "A worker is entitled during normal office hours to inspect any
-- record relating to the worker kept by his or her employer under this section." Fork F12: s 10(5) is read as a
-- worker's right against the present employer; for a former worker the Act does not say.
DECLARE `Records answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may inspect the records about you during normal office hours (s 10(5)); your employer must keep them throughout your service and for at least three years after it ends (s 10(2)(c))`
    `your former employer must keep the records about you until at least this day (s 10(2)(c)); s 10(5) gives the right to inspect to a worker against his or her employer, and does not say whether a former worker has it` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the three years after your service ended have passed (s 10(2)(c)), so the Act no longer requires the records to be kept; the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `my service has ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day it ended` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Records answer`
`the s 10 records answer for` `my service has ended` `ended on` `the day it ended` `as of` `today` MEANS
    IF NOT `my service has ended`
    THEN `yes: you may inspect the records about you during normal office hours (s 10(5)); your employer must keep them throughout your service and for at least three years after it ends (s 10(2)(c))`
    ELSE IF `today` `is on or before` `the s 10 last day`
         THEN `your former employer must keep the records about you until at least this day (s 10(2)(c)); s 10(5) gives the right to inspect to a worker against his or her employer, and does not say whether a former worker has it` `the s 10 last day`
         ELSE `the three years after your service ended have passed (s 10(2)(c)), so the Act no longer requires the records to be kept; the last day was` `the s 10 last day`
    WHERE
        `the s 10 last day` MEANS `the day it ended` `plus years` 3

§§ `s 13 -- an order from SAET`

-- s 13(1): where a worker "is not granted long service leave in accordance with this Act" or "does not receive a
-- payment to which he or she is entitled", "SAET may, on application under this section, order the employer (or former
-- employer) of the worker to grant the leave or make the payment". s 13(2): "An application ... may be made by -- (a)
-- the worker; or (b) if the worker is dead -- the worker's personal representative; or (c) with the consent of the
-- worker -- a registered association of which the worker is a member; or (d) if the employer has been found guilty of
-- failing to comply with the notice of an inspector ... -- the complainant in those proceedings or a person appearing
-- on behalf of the complainant."
DECLARE `Applicant` IS ONE OF
    `the worker himself or herself`
    `the personal representative of the worker who died`
    `a registered association the worker belongs to, with the worker's consent`
    `a registered association the worker belongs to, without the worker's consent`
    `the complainant in a prosecution in which the employer was found guilty of not complying with an inspector's notice`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Order answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may apply, and the application is within three years of the termination (s 13(4)); the s 13(2) paragraph, and the last day` HAS `the paragraph` IS A STRING, `the last day` IS A DATE
    `yes: you may apply; the service has not ended, so the three-year limit of s 13(4) has not begun; the s 13(2) paragraph is` HAS `the paragraph` IS A STRING
    `no: an order cannot be made, as the service was terminated more than three years before the application (s 13(4)); the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no: a registered association may apply only with the worker's consent (s 13(2)(c))`
    `no: a personal representative may apply only if the worker has died (s 13(2)(b))`
    `s 13(2) does not name you as someone who may apply`
    `s 13(1) does not reach this: it applies where leave was not granted in accordance with the Act or a payment due under it was not received`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN `Applicant`,
      `the worker died` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `leave was not granted or a payment was not received` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the service has ended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day it ended` IS A DATE,
      `it has been made` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE,
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Order answer`
`the s 13 answer for` `the applicant` `died` `the worker died` `not granted or not paid` `leave was not granted or a payment was not received` `ended` `the service has ended` `on` `the day it ended` `applied` `it has been made` `on` `the day of the application` `as of` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `leave was not granted or a payment was not received`
        THEN `s 13(1) does not reach this: it applies where leave was not granted in accordance with the Act or a payment due under it was not received`
        IF `the applicant` EQUALS `someone else`
        THEN `s 13(2) does not name you as someone who may apply`
        IF `the applicant` EQUALS `a registered association the worker belongs to, without the worker's consent`
        THEN `no: a registered association may apply only with the worker's consent (s 13(2)(c))`
        IF (`the applicant` EQUALS `the personal representative of the worker who died`) AND (NOT `the worker died`)
        THEN `no: a personal representative may apply only if the worker has died (s 13(2)(b))`
        IF NOT `the service has ended`
        THEN `yes: you may apply; the service has not ended, so the three-year limit of s 13(4) has not begun; the s 13(2) paragraph is` `the s 13(2) paragraph`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the deadline answer for` (`s 13(4) -- the application must be made within three years of the termination` (`the days from` `the day it ended` `to` `the s 13 last day`)) `by` `the applicant for the worker` `doing` `apply to SAET for an order` `from` `the day it ended` `ending` `the s 13 last day` `done` `it has been made` `on` `the day of the application` `as of` `today`
            WHEN `in time: done on or before the last day, which was` d THEN `yes: you may apply, and the application is within three years of the termination (s 13(4)); the s 13(2) paragraph, and the last day` `the s 13(2) paragraph` d
            WHEN `not yet done, and still in time: the last day is` d THEN `yes: you may apply, and the application is within three years of the termination (s 13(4)); the s 13(2) paragraph, and the last day` `the s 13(2) paragraph` d
            OTHERWISE `no: an order cannot be made, as the service was terminated more than three years before the application (s 13(4)); the last day was` `the s 13 last day`
    WHERE
        `the s 13 last day` MEANS `the day it ended` `plus years` 3
        `the s 13(2) paragraph` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the applicant`
            WHEN `the worker himself or herself` THEN "(a)"
            WHEN `the personal representative of the worker who died` THEN "(b)"
            WHEN `a registered association the worker belongs to, with the worker's consent` THEN "(c)"
            OTHERWISE "(d)"

-- s 13(3): "If in proceedings under this section it appears that the employer has not kept proper records relating to
-- long service leave as required by this Act and -- (a) the period of the worker's service is in issue; or (b) the
-- average number of hours worked per week by the worker over any period is in issue, SAET may, if it considers that in
-- fairness to the worker it should do so, rule that an allegation made by or on behalf of the worker as to the period
-- of the worker's service or the average number of hours worked per week over a particular period will be accepted as
-- proved in the absence of proof to the contrary."
DECLARE `What is in issue` IS ONE OF
    `the period of my service`
    `the average hours I worked each week`
    `something else`

DECLARE `Records presumption answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: SAET has ruled that what you say about this will be accepted as proved unless the employer proves otherwise (s 13(3))`
    `possibly: SAET may rule that what you say about this will be accepted as proved unless the employer proves otherwise, if it considers that fairness to you requires it (s 13(3))`
    `no: s 13(3) applies only if the employer has not kept proper long service leave records as the Act requires`
    `s 13(3) does not reach this: it covers only the period of your service and your average weekly hours`

GIVEN `the employer kept proper records` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the issue` IS A `What is in issue`,
      `SAET has so ruled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Records presumption answer`
`the s 13(3) answer for` `the employer kept proper records` `issue` `the issue` `ruled` `SAET has so ruled` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the employer kept proper records`
        THEN `no: s 13(3) applies only if the employer has not kept proper long service leave records as the Act requires`
        IF `the issue` EQUALS `something else`
        THEN `s 13(3) does not reach this: it covers only the period of your service and your average weekly hours`
        IF `SAET has so ruled`
        THEN `yes: SAET has ruled that what you say about this will be accepted as proved unless the employer proves otherwise (s 13(3))`
        OTHERWISE `possibly: SAET may rule that what you say about this will be accepted as proved unless the employer proves otherwise, if it considers that fairness to you requires it (s 13(3))`

§§ `s 12 -- an inspector's direction`

-- s 12(1) (above, with the rule). s 12(2), (3): the employer "may apply to SAET ... for a review of the notice", and
-- the application "must be made within 14 days of the receipt of the notice". s 12(4): "Pending the determination of an
-- application for review, the operation of the notice ... is suspended." s 12(6): failing to comply with the notice
-- (no review sought), or with a notice SAET confirmed within the period SAET specified, is an offence, maximum penalty
-- $5 000. s 12(7): "It is a defence to a charge of an offence under subsection (6)(a) to prove that the worker is not
-- entitled to the long service leave or the payment to which the notice relates." Fork F13: an application for review
-- made more than 14 days after receipt is not one that suspends the notice.
DECLARE `Direction answer` IS ONE OF
    `the notice states fewer than 14 days, which s 12(1) does not allow: the period must be at least 14 days`
    `the notice is suspended while SAET reviews it (s 12(4)); if SAET confirms it, your employer must comply within the period SAET specifies, on pain of an offence (s 12(6)(b), maximum penalty $5 000)`
    `your employer complied in time (s 12(1)); the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `your employer complied, but after the period stated in the notice: an offence under s 12(6)(a) (maximum penalty $5 000), unless it proves you were not entitled (s 12(7)); the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `not yet complied, and still in time: your employer must grant the leave or make the payment by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `not complied in time: an offence under s 12(6)(a) (maximum penalty $5 000), unless your employer proves you were not entitled (s 12(7)); the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the day the employer received the notice` IS A DATE,
      `the days stated` IS A NUMBER,
      `the employer applied for review` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day of the review application` IS A DATE,
      `the employer has complied` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day it complied` IS A DATE,
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Direction answer`
`the s 12 answer for a notice received on` `the day the employer received the notice` `days` `the days stated` `review` `the employer applied for review` `on` `the day of the review application` `complied` `the employer has complied` `on` `the day it complied` `as of` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the days stated` LESS THAN 14
        THEN `the notice states fewer than 14 days, which s 12(1) does not allow: the period must be at least 14 days`
        IF `the employer applied for review` AND (`the day of the review application` `is on or before` (`the day the employer received the notice` `plus days` 14))
        THEN `the notice is suspended while SAET reviews it (s 12(4)); if SAET confirms it, your employer must comply within the period SAET specifies, on pain of an offence (s 12(6)(b), maximum penalty $5 000)`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the deadline answer for` (`s 12(1) -- the employer must comply with the inspector's notice within the period stated` `the days stated`) `by` `the employer` `doing` `grant the leave or make the payment directed by the inspector` `from` `the day the employer received the notice` `ending` `the s 12 last day` `done` `the employer has complied` `on` `the day it complied` `as of` `today`
            WHEN `in time: done on or before the last day, which was` d THEN `your employer complied in time (s 12(1)); the last day was` d
            WHEN `late: done after the last day, which was` d THEN `your employer complied, but after the period stated in the notice: an offence under s 12(6)(a) (maximum penalty $5 000), unless it proves you were not entitled (s 12(7)); the last day was` d
            WHEN `not yet done, and still in time: the last day is` d THEN `not yet complied, and still in time: your employer must grant the leave or make the payment by` d
            OTHERWISE `not complied in time: an offence under s 12(6)(a) (maximum penalty $5 000), unless your employer proves you were not entitled (s 12(7)); the last day was` `the s 12 last day`
    WHERE
        `the s 12 last day` MEANS `the day the employer received the notice` `plus days` `the days stated`

§§ `ss 10, 11, 12, 14, 15 -- offences and the time to prosecute`

-- The maximum penalties written under ss 10(1), (2a), (4), (6), (7), 11(3), 12(6), 14(1), (2). s 15(1): "Offences
-- against this Act are summary offences." s 15(2): "A prosecution for an offence against this Act must be commenced
-- within three years after the date on which the offence is alleged to have been committed."
DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `not keeping the long service leave records`
    `not recording a cashing-out agreement in writing, giving me a copy, or keeping it`
    `not passing the records on to a related employer`
    `not giving me the statement before my leave`
    `not giving me the statement when my leave was cashed out`
    `obstructing an inspector or not complying with an inspector's requirement`
    `not complying with an inspector's notice to grant my leave or pay me`
    `engaging a worker knowing the worker is on long service leave, so that the worker breaches s 14(1)`
    `my own other employment in place of my employment while on long service leave`

DECLARE `Offence answer` IS ONE OF
    `a summary offence (s 15(1)); the maximum penalty in dollars, the provision, and the last day to commence a prosecution (s 15(2)), are` HAS `the maximum penalty` IS A NUMBER, `the provision` IS A STRING, `the last day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`, `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Offence answer`
`the offence answer for` `the offence` `committed on` `the day of the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not keeping the long service leave records` THEN `a summary offence (s 15(1)); the maximum penalty in dollars, the provision, and the last day to commence a prosecution (s 15(2)), are` 1000 "s 10(1)" `the s 15 last day`
    WHEN `not recording a cashing-out agreement in writing, giving me a copy, or keeping it` THEN `a summary offence (s 15(1)); the maximum penalty in dollars, the provision, and the last day to commence a prosecution (s 15(2)), are` 1000 "s 10(2a)" `the s 15 last day`
    WHEN `not passing the records on to a related employer` THEN `a summary offence (s 15(1)); the maximum penalty in dollars, the provision, and the last day to commence a prosecution (s 15(2)), are` 1000 "s 10(4)" `the s 15 last day`
    WHEN `not giving me the statement before my leave` THEN `a summary offence (s 15(1)); the maximum penalty in dollars, the provision, and the last day to commence a prosecution (s 15(2)), are` 200 "s 10(6)" `the s 15 last day`
    WHEN `not giving me the statement when my leave was cashed out` THEN `a summary offence (s 15(1)); the maximum penalty in dollars, the provision, and the last day to commence a prosecution (s 15(2)), are` 200 "s 10(7)" `the s 15 last day`
    WHEN `obstructing an inspector or not complying with an inspector's requirement` THEN `a summary offence (s 15(1)); the maximum penalty in dollars, the provision, and the last day to commence a prosecution (s 15(2)), are` 5000 "s 11(3)" `the s 15 last day`
    WHEN `not complying with an inspector's notice to grant my leave or pay me` THEN `a summary offence (s 15(1)); the maximum penalty in dollars, the provision, and the last day to commence a prosecution (s 15(2)), are` 5000 "s 12(6)" `the s 15 last day`
    WHEN `engaging a worker knowing the worker is on long service leave, so that the worker breaches s 14(1)` THEN `a summary offence (s 15(1)); the maximum penalty in dollars, the provision, and the last day to commence a prosecution (s 15(2)), are` 1000 "s 14(2)" `the s 15 last day`
    OTHERWISE `a summary offence (s 15(1)); the maximum penalty in dollars, the provision, and the last day to commence a prosecution (s 15(2)), are` 1000 "s 14(1)" `the s 15 last day`
    WHERE
        `the s 15 last day` MEANS `the day of the offence` `plus years` 3
